NextTrace GeoIP helper for IpQualityMonitor

The helper and NTrace-core are licensed under GPL-3.0-only. The installed
nexttrace-LICENSE is the upstream GPLv3 license text. NTrace-core v1.7.3 is
pinned at 40ac803ca233b0bc3d4b3bf1cacc8f7e0d8368f2. It is used only for GeoIP;
this executable performs no route probing and requires no raw-socket capability.

Linux builds apply the documented patch_linux.py to a temporary copy: bounded
PoW response/challenge sizes, cancellation, no HTTP redirects, single-attempt
authentication and safe status/Retry-After reporting. Original upstream files
and the original powclient v0.3.0 archive remain unchanged in the source bundle.

Complete corresponding source, dependency source ZIPs with their original
licenses, build scripts and build information are installed beside this notice
under /usr/share/doc/ipqualitymonitor/. Extract nexttrace-source.tar.gz and run
build-linux.sh using the verified Go 1.26.5 linux/amd64 toolchain described in
provenance.json. Go is needed only to rebuild, not to run the installed helper. The Go runtime
is covered by the separately installed nexttrace-Go-LICENSE (BSD-style).

The helper does not acquire service rights. Use of the NextTrace APIs remains
subject to the provider's authorization, quotas and service terms. API v4
credentials are supplied over private stdin and are never packaged or logged.
